{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeWedgePair","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeWedgePair","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemePolarReduction"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_wedge","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L299-L312","doc":"**The hyperbolic volume of the chimney over one wedge is `Λ(ψ)`.**\n\nThe pairing step of Milnor's subdivision, in three dimensions: two mirror\northoschemes at `½Λ(ψ)` each.  Three such wedges, at three different axes and\nwith `ψ` the three inscribed angles, would give `Λ(α)+Λ(β)+Λ(γ)` — that\nassembly is H4-5c and is OPEN, because moving a wedge off the positive `x`-axis\nneeds rotation-invariance of the base integral, which is not proved here.\n\n**Still not a statement about an ideal tetrahedron.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_wedge","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L256-L297","doc":"**H4-5b — the base integral over one wedge is `Λ(ψ)`.**\n\nTwo orthoschemes, mirror images of each other, plus a null spine. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge_subset_disk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge_subset_disk","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L228-L254","doc":"The wedge lies strictly inside the disk.\n\n`|y| < x tan ψ` and `x < R cos ψ` give `x² + y² < x²(1 + tan²ψ) = x²/cos²ψ < R²`.\nIts two far vertices are ON the circle, but the wedge is open.\n\nNo `0 < R` hypothesis: for `R ≤ 0` the wedge is empty (`0 < x < R cos ψ` is\nunsatisfiable) and the statement holds vacuously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.Lob_nonneg_of_lt_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.Lob_nonneg_of_lt_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L203-L224","doc":"**`0 ≤ Λ(ψ)` for `ψ ∈ (0, π/2)`** — read off `integral_orthoscheme`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_reflY_orthoBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.lintegral_reflY_orthoBase","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L177-L193","doc":"**The lower half of the wedge carries the same base integral as the\nupper.**  This is the `2` in `2 · ½Λ = Λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge_eq_union","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge_eq_union","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L132-L169","doc":"**The wedge splits, exactly, by the sign of `y`.**\n\n    wedge  =  orthoBase  ∪  (reflY ⁻¹' orthoBase)  ∪  spine\n\nNot an a.e. statement: this is a genuine partition of the open wedge into its\nupper half, its lower half, and the spine between them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge_fst_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge_fst_pos","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L122-L130","doc":"Every point of the wedge has positive abscissa.  Not an extra hypothesis:\n`|y| < x tan ψ` forces `x tan ψ > 0`, and `tan ψ > 0` on `(0, π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeSpine_null","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeSpine_null","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L118-L120","doc":"The spine is null — a segment in the plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_wedgeSpine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_wedgeSpine","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L115-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_wedge","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L112-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.isOpen_wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.isOpen_wedge","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L106-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeSpine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeSpine","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L101-L104","doc":"**The spine** — where the perpendicular from the apex meets the wedge's\ninterior.  A genuine part of the open wedge, and the reason the split below\nhas three pieces rather than two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedge","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**The isoceles wedge** — the OPEN Euclidean triangle with apex at the\norigin (the circumcentre), apex angle `2ψ`, and its two far vertices\n`(R cos ψ, ± R sin ψ)` on the circle of radius `R`.\n\nOne of the three pieces an inscribed triangle is cut into by joining the\ncircumcentre to its vertices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurePreserving_reflY","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurePreserving_reflY","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L75-L85","doc":"Reflection preserves Lebesgue measure on the plane: the identity on the\nfirst factor, negation on the second, and `volume` on `ℝ` is neg-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.reflY_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.reflY_apply","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.reflY","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.reflY","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OrthoschemeWedgePair.lean#L69-L71","doc":"Reflection in the `x`-axis, as a measurable equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}